    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule for owner creation, following the existing `DuplicateTelephoneException` pattern:\n\n1. **`service/DuplicateEmailException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` thrown when a created owner's lower-cased email collides with another owner's.\n\n2. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`** \u2014 added `assertEmailIsUnique(owner)`, invoked only on create (inside the `owner.isNew()` block, before the city-capacity check). It compares emails in their canonical lower-cased form via `Owner.normalizeEmail(...)`, excludes the owner being saved by id, and skips blank/null emails.\n\n3. **`rest/advice/ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateEmailException` that maps it to **HTTP 409 Conflict** with a `ProblemDetail` body, matching the other duplicate handlers.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` (create owner A with a unique email, then create owner B with the same email \u2192 expects 409) passes, and the full `./mvnw test` build is green.",
