        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, parallel addition to three existing patterns:\n\n- `DuplicateEmailException` is a faithful sibling of `DuplicateTelephoneException`/`DuplicateHouseholdException` \u2014 same package, same structure, same message style.\n- `assertEmailIsUnique` sits in the service layer right beside `assertTelephoneIsUnique` and `assertHouseholdIsUnique`, using the identical `findAll().stream()` + exclude-self-by-id + `normalizeX` idiom those methods already use (and that `countNamesakes`/`generateCustomerCode` share). It reuses the pre-existing `Owner.normalizeEmail`.\n- It is wired into `saveOwner` in the same create-only block as `assertCityHasCapacity`, matching how the other uniqueness checks are gated.\n- The `ExceptionControllerAdvice` handler mirrors the surrounding 409 handlers exactly (constant message, `detailBuild`, `warn` log, `HttpStatus.CONFLICT`).\n\nLogic is in the right unit, nothing is duplicated beyond the deliberate symmetry with its siblings, and no class is becoming a catch-all. A maintainer of this codebase would find it natural."
